The critical blocker is resolved. The observer WGSL was reduced from 50KB (1844 lines) to 10KB (224 lines) by writing a clean compact shader from scratch. The game now runs at 373 FPS.
What was done:
1. Identified root cause: The Intel Arc A770 WGSL compiler has a ~35KB limit. The accumulated observer shader (legacy + field + hybrid + 16 Mandelbulb materials + noise functions + letter rendering + Cook-Torrance + reflection tracing + radiance gradient) exceeded this limit.
2. Wrote compact_observer.wgsl from scratch with only what the field observer needs:
   * Bindings, params, cell accessors (~30 lines)
   * Trilinear field sampling (pseudo_sdf, phi, normal, surface_type) (~80 lines)
   * Field distance with w-aperture (~15 lines)
   * Tone mapping (~10 lines)
   * Pattern functions (floor, ceiling, wall, object albedo) (~35 lines)
   * Shade_hit dispatcher (~30 lines)
   * Main ray march (~25 lines)
